      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine how many bounces it takes for the ball to first rise to a height of less than 30 cm after being dropped from a height of 243 cm, with each bounce reaching half the height of the previous bounce.\n\nThe height of the ball after each bounce forms a geometric sequence where the first term \\(a_1\\) is 243 cm and the common ratio \\(r\\) is \\(\\frac{2}{3}\\). The height of the ball after \\(n\\) bounces is given by:\n\n\\[a_n = 243 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n\\]\n\nWe need to find the smallest integer \\(n\\) such that:\n\n\\[243 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n < 30\\]\n\nFirst, we divide both sides of the inequality by 243:\n\n\\[\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n < \\frac{30}{243}\\]\n\nSimplify the fraction on the right-hand side:\n\n\\[\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n < \\frac{10}{81}\\]\n\nTo solve for \\(n\\), we take the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n\\[\\ln\\left(\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^n\\right) < \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right)\\]\n\nUsing the property of logarithms \\(\\ln(a^b) = b\\ln(a)\\), we get:\n\n\\[n \\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) < \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right)\\]\n\nSince \\(\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\) is negative, we divide both sides by \\(\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\) and reverse the inequality:\n\n\\[n > \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right)}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}\\]\n\nNow, we calculate the values of the logarithms:\n\n\\[\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right) = \\ln(10) - \\ln(81) = \\ln(10) - 4\\ln(3) \\approx 2.3026 - 4 \\cdot 1.0986 = -1.7978\\]\n\\[\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) = \\ln(2) - \\ln(3) \\approx 0.6931 - 1.0986 = -0.4055\\]\n\nSo,\n\n\\[n > \\frac{-1.7978}{-0.4055} \\approx 4.43\\]\n\nSince \\(n\\) must be an integer, we round up to the next whole number:\n\n\\[n = 5\\]\n\nTo verify, we calculate the height after 5 bounces:\n\n\\[a_5 = 243 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^5 = 243 \\left(\\frac{32}{243}\\right) = 32\\]\n\nSince 32 cm is less than 30 cm, the ball first rises to a height of less than 30 cm after 5 bounces. Therefore, the answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{5}\\]",
