      "text": "The height of the ball after each bounce can be represented as a geometric sequence. The first term, $a_1$, is $243$ cm, and the common ratio, $r$, is $\\frac{2}{3}$. The height after the $n$th bounce is given by $a_n = 243 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{n-1}$.\n\nWe need to find the smallest $n$ such that $a_n < 30$. This inequality can be written as:\n\n\\[243 \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{n-1} < 30\\]\n\nTo solve for $n$, we first divide both sides by $243$:\n\n\\[\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{n-1} < \\frac{30}{243}\\]\n\nSimplifying the right side:\n\n\\[\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{n-1} < \\frac{10}{81}\\]\n\nTaking the natural logarithm of both sides:\n\n\\[\\ln\\left(\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^{n-1}\\right) < \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right)\\]\n\nUsing the property of logarithms that $\\ln(a^b) = b \\ln(a)$:\n\n\\[(n-1) \\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) < \\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right)\\]\n\nSince $\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)$ is negative, we need to divide both sides by $\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)$ and reverse the inequality:\n\n\\[n-1 > \\frac{\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right)}{\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}\\]\n\nCalculating the values of the logarithms:\n\n\\[\\ln\\left(\\frac{10}{81}\\right) = \\ln(10) - \\ln(81) = \\ln(10) - 4\\ln(3)\\]\n\\[\\ln\\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right) = \\ln(2) - \\ln(3)\\]\n\nSo the inequality becomes:\n\n\\[n-1 > \\frac{\\ln(10) - 4\\ln(3)}{\\ln(2) - \\ln(3)}\\]\n\nUsing approximate values for the logarithms (approximation: $\\ln(10) \\approx 2.3026$, $\\ln(3) \\approx 1.0986$, $\\ln(2) \\approx 0.6931$):\n\n\\[n-1 > \\frac{2.3026 - 4 \\cdot 1.0986}{0.6931 - 1.0986} = \\frac{2.3026 - 4.3944}{-0.4055} = \\frac{-2.0918}{-0.4055} \\approx 5.16\\]\n\nTherefore:\n\n\\[n-1 > 5.16\\]\n\nAdding 1 to both sides:\n\n\\[n > 6.16\\]\n\nSince $n$ must be an integer, the smallest integer greater than $6.16$ is $7$. So, the ball first rises less than $30$ cm after the $7$th bounce. Thus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{7}\\]\n```python\n# Let's verify the calculation using Python\n\n# Initial height of the ball\ninitial_height = 243\n\n# Common ratio for the bounce\nratio = 2 / 3\n\n# Function to calculate height after n bounces\ndef height_after_n_bounces(n):\n    return initial_height * (ratio ** (n - 1))\n\n# Find the smallest n such that the height after n bounces is less than 30 cm\nn = 1\nwhile height_after_n_bounces(n) >= 30:\n    n += 1\n\nprint(n)\n```",
